From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tom Englund <tomenglund26@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 19:40:50 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] nvidia-drm: don't keep a flip's semaphore in later CRTC
 states

Duplicating a CRTC state copied each layer's config including syncParams, which
are only reset for planes that are part of the new commit. A flip ignores them
for the other planes, but a modeset request sends the config of every layer on
its heads. With a modeset on one CRTC and a commit leaving out a plane on
another, that plane's flip waited on the semaphore of an old flip, until a
later fence happened to release it or the channel idle timed out.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

diff --git a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
index 0533136c..85e7e2fe 100644
--- a/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
+++ b/kernel-open/nvidia-drm/nvidia-drm-crtc.c
@@ -2473,6 +2473,13 @@ static inline bool nv_drm_crtc_duplicate_req_head_modeset_config(
     for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(old->layerRequestedConfig); i++) {
         new->layerRequestedConfig[i].config =
             old->layerRequestedConfig[i].config;
+        /*
+         * These belong to the commit that set them. A modeset sends the config
+         * of planes that aren't part of its commit too, and would wait on an
+         * old semaphore.
+         */
+        memset(&new->layerRequestedConfig[i].config.syncParams, 0,
+               sizeof(new->layerRequestedConfig[i].config.syncParams));
     }
 
     return true;
